{
  "_notes": "Castilian Spanish (es-ES) taxonomy. 10 grammar + 10 vocabulary subs, mirroring FR/PT structure so the runtime stays language-agnostic. Key Spanish-specific decisions: (1) Replaced FR's 'relative_pronouns' sub with 'ser_vs_estar' — the single biggest Spanish-learner struggle, same move PT made. Relative pronouns (que, donde, cuyo) live inside 'complex_sentences'. (2) Past tenses center on pretérito indefinido vs imperfecto plus pretérito perfecto (he hablado) — Castilian uses pretérito perfecto productively for today/this-week, unlike most LatAm varieties. (3) Subjunctive includes imperfecto and pluscuamperfecto de subjuntivo for B2/C1 hypotheticals and the cuando+subjunctive future-reference trigger. (4) 'pronouns_personal' covers OD/OI/leísmo plus the Castilian-specific vosotros/ustedes split and gustar-type verbs. (5) Prepositions sub leads with por vs para — the headline preposition contrast. (6) Vocabulary patterns localized to Spain: DNI/NIE/Hacienda/Seguridad Social/Renfe/médico de cabecera replace FR's CAF/impôts. Register sub captures tú/usted (Castilian tutea more freely), vosotros and slang (vale, guay, molar, tío/tía). Pattern lists are scoped to what the starter seed bank exercises; expand them as the bank grows.",
